## Installation

### Requirements

- Python {{ python_version.split('.')[0] }}.{{ python_version.split('.')[1] }}
- uv

```sh
brew install uv
```

### Install from source

Clone the repository and enter the project directory:

```sh
git clone https://github.com/dkidney/{{ project_name }}.git
cd {{ project_name }}
```

Install the project and its development dependencies:

```sh
uv sync --dev
```

Install the Git hooks:

```sh
uv run pre-commit install
```

Pre-commit will now run the configured checks automatically when you commit changes.

#### Running checks manually

Run all pre-commit hooks against the entire repository:

```sh
uv run pre-commit run --all-files
```

Run the test suite:

```sh
uv run pytest
```

#### Updating dependencies

If you change dependencies in pyproject.toml, update the lockfile:

uv lock

Commit the updated uv.lock file along with your changes.

If a pre-commit hook modifies a file, review the changes, stage them, and run the commit again.

